# Top-level pins for the Python binding jobs on Python 3.10 and newer:
# python.yml (3.10 and 3.12 rows), ci.yml test-python and nightly.yml.
# The Python 3.8 row of python.yml installs py38/python-bindings-py38.txt
# instead, because the pytest releases that fix GHSA-6w46-j5rx-g56g (9.0.3 and
# later) need Python 3.10+.
#
# One file serves every Python (3.10 to the newest matrix row) and OS those
# jobs run on, and pip-compile drops a requirement whose environment marker is
# false on the machine that compiles. So every dependency that holds only on
# some Python or OS is listed here unconditionally, with an exact pin: a
# pure-Python wheel that is harmless where the marker is false. Any compile of
# this file, on any Python (Dependabot compiles on its own), then resolves the
# same package set, and scripts/check_release_workflow.py fails a .txt whose set
# differs.
#   colorama           pytest, Windows only
#   exceptiongroup     pytest, Python < 3.11
#   tomli              pytest and maturin, Python < 3.11
#   typing-extensions  exceptiongroup, Python < 3.13
# Compile it on the OLDEST Python it serves (3.10).
#
# Refresh recipe: docs/CI.md, "Hashed Python requirements".
maturin==1.15.0
pytest==9.1.1
colorama==0.4.6
exceptiongroup==1.3.1
tomli==2.5.0
typing-extensions==4.16.0
